      "node_id": "kg_doc_4",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "Le Médecin malgré lui (] ; \"The doctor/physician in spite of himself\") is a farce by Molière first presented in 1666 (published as a manuscript in early 1667) at le théâtre du Palais-Royal by la Troupe du Roi. The play is one of several plays by Molière to center on Sganarelle, a character that Molière himself portrayed, and is a comedic satire of 17th century French medicine.",
